+/* Periodic report, thread 0 only, designed so it costs almost nothing INSIDE the measured window.
+ *
+ * The atexit-only reporter made the evidence chain depend on a CLEAN shutdown: SIGKILL from a hung
+ * arm, a crashed server or a timeout skips atexit, leaves no counter line, and the analyzer marks a
+ * perfectly good packed arm INVALID. A periodic line fixes that, but stderr on Android is a pipe to
+ * adb and a blocking write during a measured request is not free even when it is 0.0004% of a step.
+ *
+ * So: ONE line at graph BONSAI_PK_FIRST (default 1 - the floor, since no arm can run fewer than one
+ * graph), then every BONSAI_PK_EVERY graphs (default 512), a handful of prints per arm rather than
+ * two dozen. Graph 1 always lands during warmup, well outside any measured window.
+ *
